 "answer": "**No, it is strongly advised that she skips her outdoor morning walk today.** \n\nSingapore is currently experiencing a severe haze situation, with the 24-hour Pollutant Standards Index (PSI) forecast to range between **150 and 230 (Unhealthy to Very Unhealthy)**. \n\nOfficial health advisories for the elderly explicitly recommend that:\n* **Elderly, pregnant women, and children should minimize outdoor activity** when PSI levels reach the Unhealthy to Very Unhealthy range.\n* If she must step outside, she should check the real-time 1-hour PM2.5 readings via the [myENV app or haze microsite](http://www.haze.gov.sg), and avoid all outdoor physical exertion if levels spike. \n\nGiven her age, it is much safer for her to stay indoors and exercise safely inside today until the air quality improves.",
